    "bodyMarkdown": "# Front-Door Triage Card\n\n**Rule:** accept only when **ownership + safety + lock/data status + viable route + storage** are sufficiently known.\n\n## 1. Ownership\n- Who owns it?\n- Is the person/business authorised to transfer it?\n- Record source + signature/authority.\n- Record serial/IMEI where present.\n**STOP:** unclear ownership, altered/missing identifiers that raise concern, or conflicting story.\n\n## 2. Safety\n- swollen/leaking/hot/smoking battery?\n- fire/flood/severe crush/puncture?\n- pest/biological contamination?\n- damaged mains wiring/plug/internal PSU?\n**STOP/REJECT:** immediate lithium or electrical hazard. Do not charge.\n\n## 3. Locks\n- Apple Activation Lock / ABM MDM?\n- Android FRP / Knox Guard / carrier block?\n- Windows Autopilot / organisation enrolment?\n- Chromebook enterprise enrolment?\n- BIOS/supervisor password / Absolute?\n**STOP:** unresolved ownership/management lock unless legitimate release is documented.\n\n## 4. Viability\n- exact model / CPU / RAM / storage?\n- supported OS/security life?\n- obvious structural or liquid damage?\n- replacement battery/charger available?\n- likely resale > parts/scrap + labour + risk?\n\n## 5. Route\nChoose one **before acceptance**:\n- REFURBISH\n- PARTS\n- DONATE/REUSE PARTNER\n- DOWNSTREAM RECYCLE\n- REJECT / OWNER RETAINS\n\nIf no credible route exists, **do not accept**.\n\n## 6. Data\nAll accepted data-bearing devices:\n**UNWIPED — RESTRICTED**\nuntil sanitisation + verification are recorded.\n\n## 7. Storage\nIs there a labelled safe position available now?\nIf not, reject/defer intake rather than create an uncontrolled pile.\n"
